public class ValidAnagram {

    public static boolean isAnagram(String str1, String str2) {

        // Convert to lowercase
        str1 = str1.toLowerCase();
        str2 = str2.toLowerCase();

        // Remove spaces
        str1 = str1.replace(" ", "");
        str2 = str2.replace(" ", "");

        // If lengths differ -> not anagram
        if (str1.length() != str2.length()) {
            return false;
        }

        // Bucket array for 26 letters
        int[] counts = new int[26];

        // Increase count for str1
        for (int i = 0; i < str1.length(); i++) {
            counts[str1.charAt(i) - 'a']++;
        }

        // Decrease count for str2
        for (int i = 0; i < str2.length(); i++) {
            counts[str2.charAt(i) - 'a']--;
        }

        // Check all buckets
        for (int count : counts) {
            if (count != 0) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        String str1 = "dormitory";
        String str2 = "dirty room";

        System.out.println(isAnagram(str1, str2));
    }
}
--------------------------------------------
Important Logic
Why charAt(i) - 'a' ?
Example:

'b' - 'a' = 1
'c' - 'a' = 2
'z' - 'a' = 25

So:

index 0 → a
index 1 → b
index 25 → z

That’s why array size is 26.

Time Complexity

O(n)

Space Complexity

O(1) because array size is fixed (26).
